# Build products of the local toolchain are SHIPPING artifacts here (the project's deliverable is a
# binary + its SPIR-V on a machine with no package manager), so *.exe / *.spv are deliberately NOT
# ignored. What is ignored is anything that is not source, not a measurement, and not a product:
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# The reference checkpoints used by the alignment tools. They are downloads, not work products, and one
# of them is 41 MiB; the reports cite their SHA and the logs they produced, which is what belongs here.
runs/*.gguf
runs/*.safetensors

# Model weights are tens of GB and are NEVER a work product, anywhere in the tree (the engine is pointed
# at them at run time). Block them globally, plus the conventional local weights / toolchain directories.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
models/
toolchain/

# The frozen pre-P1 snapshot binary. It is kept on disk only because runs/diff_pre_p1_v2.txt was measured
# against it; it is NOT rebuilt from current source, NOT shipped in dist, and predates the relative-path
# desensitisation, so it must never be committed. (*.exe is otherwise a shipping artifact, see top.)
runtime_vk/bonsai_vk_baseline_v1.exe

# Live serve-daemon stdout/stderr: operational logs of a running server, not measurement evidence. They
# grow while the server runs and record the run-time model path argument, so they stay local.
runs/serve_daemon_*.log

# Stray build logs from a batch-script bug (uncited, superseded by runs/build_release_v1.log).
runtime_vk/..runsbuild_*.log

# Editor / OS droppings.
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
